    "## 3. OULAD Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "**What we're building:** `(student_id, skill_id, correct, timestamp)` interaction sequences.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key design decision — use assessments as interactions, not VLE clicks:**\n",
    "VLE clicks don't have binary correct/incorrect labels per interaction. Assigning them\n",
    "the label of a future assessment causes leakage (all clicks in a window share the same label).\n",
    "Instead, we use **each assessment attempt as one interaction**, which gives genuine per-event\n",
    "correctness. This is exactly what the PLRS FYP used (val AUC 0.7692).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Skill proxy:** `assessment_type` (TMA, CMA, Exam) × `code_module` — gives ~200 meaningful skill buckets.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Join logic:**\n",
    "- `assessments.csv` — metadata: `id_assessment, code_module, code_presentation, assessment_type, date`\n",
    "- `studentAssessment.csv` — per-student scores: `id_student, id_assessment, score`\n"
   ]
  },
